  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered and no validation response deadline is pending; the voluntary independent-validation budget is exhausted. The synthesis therefore uses the supplied discovery ledger plus previously delivered validation. Returned estimates and intervals remain signed to each claim direction: a positive signed value means the exposed level has a more negative outcome_001 value, i.e. stronger composite dependency, and the decision rule is a signed lower 95% bound above +0.15 composite dependency-score units. Supported findings: four large binary supplied-dataset associations stand out, each well above the 0.15 threshold and independently validated. feature_037=1 versus 0 is supported in H16/R13/R22 with discovery about +0.80 and validation about +0.82; feature_010=0 versus 1 is supported in H39/R12/R35 with discovery about +0.83 and validation about +0.79; feature_002=0 versus 1 is supported in H86/R51/R72 with discovery about +0.81 and validation about +0.82; feature_027=1 versus 0 is supported in H139/R109/R111 with discovery about +0.77 and validation about +0.86. These are associations only: opaque labels, unknown predictor correlations, and non-experimental conditioning prevent causal, mechanistic, clinical-role, or generalizability claims. They also remain large in many eligibility and stratum restrictions, including H292-H294 within feature_063=0, so the major tracks are not removed by conditioning on feature_063 status. Negative findings are broad. Constructed markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 are null as main effects and modifiers (H1-H3, H8-H10). feature_024 level_002 versus level_001 is null, and its feature_007 interaction is unsupported after validation (H7, H11). Most low-prevalence binary predictors are below threshold or null, including feature_041, feature_031, feature_023, feature_048, feature_060, feature_035, feature_033, feature_016, feature_013, feature_022, feature_028, feature_050, feature_064, feature_043, and feature_001. feature_053 numeric contrasts are below threshold, feature_046 comparisons are not supported, and feature_003 is not a robust independent residual track: overall and many conditional contrasts are below threshold or attenuate under validation. Apparent modification by feature_040 or feature_030, especially for feature_002, is not validated; H186/H211 show that a feature_040-related interaction does not survive validation. Null interactions and null subgroup findings do not prove exact independence, and insufficient-cell analyses are non-evidence rather than null evidence. Unresolved uncertainty centers on feature_063. The overall claim H24/R214 is borderline: signed estimate about +0.24 but lower bound +0.145, just below threshold, so it should remain unresolved. Several selected feature_063 contrasts in reference backgrounds have lower bounds just above +0.15 and are accepted only as weak context-specific residual associations (H286, H287, H290), not as a corrected independent track because the feature_063 family has large unadjusted multiplicity, predictor-selected conditioning, and small cells in several contrasts. In active major strata, feature_063 is not supported (H288, H289). H291 is borderline positive in a low feature_040 subset but below threshold and remains deferred. H295 feature_003 in the clean feature_063=0 core is positive but below threshold, reinforcing feature_003 nonrobustness while leaving that narrow claim deferred. H296/H298 feature_063 and feature_003 jointly present cells are small and unsupported. The most informative next discovery analysis is the newly proposed feature_063=1 versus 0 contrast restricted to the all-reference core feature_010=0, feature_037=0, feature_002=0, feature_027=0, feature_003=0. This separates feature_063 from feature_003 and the four major tracks; a threshold-positive lower bound would strengthen a weak dataset-specific residual feature_063 association, while attenuation or insufficient cells would support leaving feature_063 borderline rather than promoting it. If external data were available, pre-specified validation and a multiplicity-aware joint model would be preferable; within this run, that core restriction is the best remaining discovery step. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations only.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 21 final synthesis. No new validation deadline; independent validation budget exhausted. Discovery-only follow-up proposed. Direction convention: all claims use signed intervals; positive signed value = exposed level more negative outcome_001, stronger dependency; accept only if signed lower bound > +0.15. Supported major supplied-dataset binary associations: feature_037=1 vs 0 (H16, R13, R22), feature_010=0 vs 1 (H39, R12, R35), feature_002=0 vs 1 (H86, R51, R72), feature_027=1 vs 0 (H139, R109, R111). All large, validated, and persist within many restrictions including feature_063 strata. Associations only, not causal or generalizable. Negative: feature_007/058/015 null; feature_024 null; feature_041, feature_031, feature_023, feature_048, feature_060, feature_035, feature_033, feature_016, feature_013, feature_022, feature_028, feature_050, feature_064, feature_043, feature_001 not supported; feature_053 below threshold; feature_046 not supported; feature_003 not robust; feature_040/feature_030 effect modification unsupported, especially H186/H211 validation for feature_002 by feature_040. Unresolved: H24 overall feature_063 is borderline (R214 lower 0.145); H286/H287/H290 accepted only weak context-specific feature_063 residuals; H288/H289 fail in active major strata; H291 borderline deferred; H295 feature_003 in clean feature_063=0 core positive but below threshold, deferred; H296/H298 small joint feature_003/feature_063 cells unsupported. Proposed next analysis: feature_063=1 vs 0 within feature_010=0, feature_037=0, feature_002=0, feature_027=0, feature_003=0, parent H24. Interpretation rule: if lower bound > 0.15, supports a weak dataset-specific residual feature_063 association; if attenuated, supports unresolved borderline status. Best external next steps if available: pre-specified validation and multiplicity-aware joint modeling; neither supports causality or biology. All results are supplied-dataset associations only."
